; One of each run of the same consonant (the rules give LITTLE as T T). Cards pass through, except that a consonant
; (code 19 and up, 10 x code as the rules give it) the same as the card just before it is dropped. A card below 0
; (a word's end, a pause) clears what came before. Only the rules' words have such runs; the exceptions' phonemes and
; the letters' names have none, so they pass through unchanged.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            rec     INP   x        03-22: a card: a repeated consonant is dropped
  04                    CLA   x
  05                    TAC   clr
  06                    SUB   prev
  07                    TAC   keep
  08                    SUB   00
  09                    TAC   same
  10                    JMP   keep
  11            same    CLA   x
  12                    SUB   c190
  13                    TAC   keep
  14                    JMP   rec
  15            clr     CLA   z
  16                    STO   prev
  17                    OUT   x
  18                    JMP   rec
  19            keep    CLA   x
  20                    STO   prev
  21                    OUT   x
  22                    JMP   rec
  30            x       DATA  0
  31            prev    DATA  0
  32            z       DATA  0
  33            c190    DATA  190
